{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/kirnbergerIII"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kirnbergerIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by ¼ of the syntonic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comma, equal to ⁴√5 ≈ 696.578 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schisma (32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining seven"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one schisma equals one Pythagorean comma."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The four quarter-comma fifths make C–E a pure major third (5:4). Published in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Die Kunst des reinen Satzes in der Musik"}]},{"text":", Part II.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kirnberger III (Johann Philipp Kirnberger, 1779)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kirnbergeriii"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}